---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Hello World">
  <article>
    <h1>Hello World</h1>
    <p>
      This is a sample blog post for the slop-detect Astro example. It keeps
      styling minimal so the scanner focuses on structure and copy, not theme
      flourishes.
    </p>
    <p>
      Real posts would live here as static routes or content collections. For
      this demo, one page is enough to show how a built Astro site can be
      scored after deploy or preview.
    </p>
    <p>
      Run <code>bun run build</code>, serve the output, then point slop-detect
      at the URL to see your slop score.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>